# The image only ever builds the server bundle. The Dockerfile copies exactly
# package.json, package-lock.json, tsconfig.json, server/ and shared/ — so
# everything else (9MB of Illustrator sources, the Expo app, docs, scripts)
# was being shipped to the daemon for nothing.
#
# Deny-all then allow, rather than a blocklist: a new top-level folder joins
# the context only when someone adds it here on purpose.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!server
!server/**
!shared
!shared/**

# Never, even inside the allowed trees.
**/node_modules
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
